I contributed to the CBIM Problem Canvas with my teammates and worked mainly on Sections 1.1 and 1.2. In 1.1, I loaded and inspected the retail dataset, checked its structure, missing values, data types, and basic statistics, and wrote the main business observations. In 1.2, I analysed monthly revenue for all five categories, created the category trend chart, and identified the biggest decline and the most consistent category. From Saketh’s sections, I learned how product level revenue and discount analysis can explain the reasons behind a category’s performance. From Raghunandan’s sections, I learned how day-of-week and monthly patterns can be connected to promotion timing and the final business briefing. Working with the team also helped me understand that the project is not only about coding,x` each analysis should lead to a clear business insight, support the stakeholder’s decision, and suggest a useful action for the supplier meeting as well more clearly.